        "outcome": "concerns",
        "summary": "The design has five concrete gaps involving concurrent deletion, retry semantics, post-save UI consistency, unbounded public writes, and demonstration isolation.",
        "findings": [
          {
            "id": "concurrent-delete-can-restore-orphan",
            "severity": "high",
            "category": "correctness",
            "message": "Two concurrent deletes can both capture the same body. After one request successfully removes both stores, the other can observe that its D1 delete affected no row and restore the captured R2 body, leaving an orphan object after a successful delete. Compensation must be conditional on this request still owning the row/state it is compensating.",
            "sourceRanges": [
              {
                "path": "openspec/changes/sac-246/design.md",
                "startLine": 81,
                "endLine": 83
              },
              {
                "path": "openspec/changes/sac-246/design.md",
                "startLine": 147,
                "endLine": 147
              },
              {
                "path": "openspec/changes/sac-246/specs/text-snippet-shelf/spec.md",
                "startLine": 48,
                "endLine": 48
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "delete-retry-state-is-contradictory",
            "severity": "medium",
            "category": "consistency",
            "message": "If a delete succeeds but its response is lost, a retry receives 404. The general delete flow says every failure keeps the current state and reports that the snippet was not deleted, while the failure table says an absent row clears stale browser data. The design must define one idempotent replay outcome so the UI does not retain and misreport an already-deleted snippet.",
            "sourceRanges": [
              {
                "path": "openspec/changes/sac-246/design.md",
                "startLine": 57,
                "endLine": 57
              },
              {
                "path": "openspec/changes/sac-246/design.md",
                "startLine": 83,
                "endLine": 84
              },
              {
                "path": "openspec/changes/sac-246/design.md",
                "startLine": 134,
                "endLine": 134
              },
              {
                "path": "openspec/changes/sac-246/design.md",
                "startLine": 138,
                "endLine": 138
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "saved-title-depends-on-fallible-refresh",
            "severity": "medium",
            "category": "completeness",
            "message": "After storage returns 201, the browser relies on separate list and read requests to expose the new snippet, but no fallback uses the metadata already returned by POST. If either follow-up fails, the form may be cleared while the successfully saved title is absent, contrary to the requirement that it appear after save succeeds.",
            "sourceRanges": [
              {
                "path": "openspec/changes/sac-246/design.md",
                "startLine": 55,
                "endLine": 55
              },
              {
                "path": "openspec/changes/sac-246/design.md",
                "startLine": 76,
                "endLine": 76
              },
              {
                "path": "openspec/changes/sac-246/specs/text-snippet-shelf/spec.md",
                "startLine": 9,
                "endLine": 9
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "public-writes-have-no-size-bound",
            "severity": "medium",
            "category": "security",
            "message": "The unauthenticated temporary URL permits mutation, yet the design defines no title, body, or request-size limit and only says large bodies should be streaming-compatible where practical. An accidental or hostile oversized save can exhaust Worker memory or consume temporary storage; the API should define enforceable bounds and a clear rejection response.",
            "sourceRanges": [
              {
                "path": "openspec/changes/sac-246/design.md",
                "startLine": 61,
                "endLine": 61
              },
              {
                "path": "openspec/changes/sac-246/design.md",
